Subject: [PATCH] arm: airoha: select the Linux kernel image header for AN7581

Stock U-Boot boots the chainloader as a Linux kernel and needs the ARM64
Image header that reports the runtime size. The vendor loader build selects
it; the upstream AN7581 target does not.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-airoha/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-airoha/Kconfig
@@ -22,5 +22,6 @@ config TARGET_AN7581
 	bool "Airoha AN7581 SoC"
 	select ARM64
+	select LINUX_KERNEL_IMAGE_HEADER
 	help
 	  The Airoha EN7581 is a ARM-based SoC with a quad-core Cortex-A7
 	  including NEON and GPU, Mali-450 graphics, several DDR3 options,
